---
<section class="page wrap">
  <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/colophon/">‹ How this site is built</a></nav>
  <header class="list-head">
    <h1 class="page-title">Sources and corrections</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      Every number on this site renders from one source file, synced to the résumé dated
      <strong>{{ facts.meta.resume_rev }}</strong>. A build check refuses any page that contradicts it.
      Below: the sources, and the corrections made along the way.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="case-body">
    <section class="case-sec" id="headline">
      <h2>Headline numbers</h2>
      <div class="table-panel">
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Stated as</th><th>Where it's explained</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {%- for r in facts.receipts %}
              <tr>
                <td>{{ r.label }}</td>
                <td class="num">{{ r.value }}</td>
                <td class="mono"><a href="{{ r.anchor }}">{{ r.anchor }}</a></td>
              </tr>
              {%- endfor %}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="scroll-hint">Swipe sideways to see the whole table.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-sec" id="systems">
      <h2>Systems and the number each one moved</h2>
      <div class="table-panel">
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>System</th><th>Result on record</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {%- for s in facts.systems %}
              <tr>
                <td class="mono dim">{{ s.id }}</td>
                <td><a href="{{ s.link }}">{{ s.name }}</a></td>
                <td class="num">{{ s.proof }}</td>
              </tr>
              {%- endfor %}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="scroll-hint">Swipe sideways to see the whole table.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-sec" id="corrections">
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <div class="prose"><p>Earlier revisions of this site stated some of these numbers differently. The build now refuses the superseded forms. Superseded strings are written with numeric entities below so that the check can keep forbidding them while this page names them.</p></div>
      <div class="table-panel" style="margin-top:16px;">
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Previously stated</th><th>Now stated</th><th>Since</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="dim">"&#60;0.5&#37; variance vs Finance"</td><td class="num">&lt;1% variance vs Finance</td><td class="mono dim">2026-07-09</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="dim">"4&#45;org severity-2 command"</td><td class="num">4-team cross-org severity-2 command</td><td class="mono dim">2026-07-09</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="dim">Program outcomes credited to the customer-health agent</td><td class="num">Agent: days → &lt;2 min · program: ~50% fewer aging issues, ~16% faster mitigation</td><td class="mono dim">2026-07-10</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="dim">"7&#54; tests · 1&#55; PRs · ~4&#215; partner coverage"</td><td class="num">Counts dropped as stale · ~80–90% more partner accounts tracked</td><td class="mono dim">2026-08-21</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="dim">"4&#55; datasets profiled hourly"</td><td class="num">400+ production datasets profiled hourly</td><td class="mono dim">2026-08-21</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="dim">"MCP tool servers &#215;2"</td><td class="num">Four reusable MCP servers, one of which lets Copilot query any live operations dashboard</td><td class="mono dim">2026-08-21</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="dim">"5&#43; downstream consumers" for the account embeddings</td><td class="num">Productionizing with a first consumer — restated downward to match the résumé</td><td class="mono dim">2026-08-21</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="scroll-hint">Swipe sideways to see the whole table.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-sec" id="how">
      <h2>How this works</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Every number, date, and link renders from <code>facts.yaml</code>, and
          <code>scripts/receipts-lint.mjs</code> scans the built HTML on every deploy: required claims must
          appear, superseded claims must not, internal jargon fails the build, and every internal link must
          resolve. The mechanics are on the <a href="/colophon/">colophon</a>; the check itself is
          <a href="{{ facts.identity.github }}/sarthak0501.github.io">in the repository</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>
